{
  "case_id": "2016-16-142",
  "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Adam G. Unikowski)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner's brother obtained nearly\n$270,000 in proceeds from the sales of Polar Pure.\nPetitioner obtained nothing, yet the government seeks to\nhold him jointly and severally liable for the entire\namount. That position contradicts the text, structure,\nhistory, and purpose of Section 853."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0000-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF ADAM G. UNIKOWSKY\nON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But doesn't it seem that\nthere's some back and forth about what's new and what's\nold in the government's theory, is that part of what's\nchanged in the government's theory or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Would our -- how would\nour ruling here affect the RICO forfeiture statute,\n1963?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Did the government ever\ntry to invoke (d) here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: It does have a number of\ncourts -- courts of appeals on its side, doesn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: This is a -- a bit off\ntopic, but the statute refers to proceeds that the\nperson obtained directly or indirectly.\nDo you have a view as to what that\n\"indirectly\" is doing there and what it encompasses?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: If -- if they both have -- was carrying it, they both have the duffle bag and all that, and you say, well, they are both liable"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher (Government)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And in that circumstance, I didn't say they are both liable for the forfeiture. The government doesn't have to prove which of them is responsible for the cash."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So do you have to show one of these five preconditions in (p)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher (Government)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLETCHER: To invoke (p), (p) is a procedure that allows the government to for -- forfeit specific substitute assets in a defendant's hands, a car or a house, something like that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But -- but it's odd that you use P, which would apply to substitute property -- you apply it even though this particular defendant or the particular person did nothing himself to place the proceeds beyond the reach of -- of the court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher (Government)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLETCHER: That's correct. If you were in a situation where the traceable proceeds aren't available, then you're in a joint-and-several liability situation --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Where does it say that? I mean -- I didn't take that point -- you're saying the word \"property\" in A1 is the tainted property."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm having trouble with just one component of your argument, many, but one that for the moment, which is the one that led the -- the one court who's against -- MR. FLETCHER: Yeah. JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- on this this issue was the courier who receives 50 dollars a week or 50 dollars a trip to deliver drugs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher (Government)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0001-0011",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLETCHER: In order to forfeit substitute property under (p), and -- and -- before you continue, I just want to put on the table that our view is the government doesn't have to invoke (p). It can also obtain a forfeiture money judgment if the directly forfeitable property isn't available."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: And when you say that you've shown that, what do you mean?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Why not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One way that we can definitely do that is through the substitute assets provision in Section 853(p). As we explain, we think you can apply the same principles of attributed liability to a co-conspirator's act of dealing in cash or laundering proceeds or otherwise --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the way the government has litigated this case throughout was its theory that Section 853(a)(1), and specifically the word \"obtain,\" was enough to establish joint-and-several liability. So what the government has said is that it uses the word \"obtained,\" and that simply means that that imputes everyone in the conspiracy and that's enough to establish Petitioner's liability for forfeiture of any amount that was not actually forfeited from Petitioner's brother."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: So I -- I -- what's the relevance of that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. UNIKOWSKY: Right. But the fact that it's in personam versus in rem doesn't change the fact that it's the tainted property that's the object of the forfeiture, which is, in fact, the government's concession."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I thought the argument was there simply to say there isn't an old tradition of getting B, who's in the basement, and I -- and I forget where they all are at this point. Getting the courier to forfeit his own money which isn't in the bag. Okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-142",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c114cf5d33e9d8560321b3fcaa7fccf85051962def9c5741cbdc5b66eab5661c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c114cf5d33e9-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
